1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,310
This is the implementation demo for journey three.

2
00:00:03,310 --> 00:00:08,730
It is the real application and API running on this machine, with synthetic people.

3
00:00:08,730 --> 00:00:13,760
It shows how an approved mechanic saves the times they can take inspections,

4
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:17,400
and how buyers see only the times that are really free.

5
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:21,970
The mechanic signs in and opens their availability.

6
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:27,280
To add a window they open a dialog and choose a day and hours, in Eastern Time.

7
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:31,710
A start that is not on the half hour, and an end before the start,

8
00:00:31,710 --> 00:00:34,330
are refused with a list of what to fix.

9
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:38,830
Fixing them saves the window, which shows as eight half hour slots.

10
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:42,250
A second window that overlaps the first is refused,

11
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:44,670
and the dialog keeps what was typed.

12
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:49,370
Editing a window works the same way, and here the start moves earlier.

13
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,850
Now the buyer's side.

14
00:00:51,850 --> 00:00:56,790
A buyer asks for slots and gets only the half hour times inside the mechanic's

15
00:00:56,790 --> 00:01:00,220
window, in universal time with the Eastern zone named.

16
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:05,360
When an administrator deactivates the mechanic, the same request returns nothing.

17
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:08,080
Approving them again brings the slots back.

18
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:11,220
Booked times are protected too.

19
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:15,630
A slot can be reserved only once, even when requests arrive together,

20
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:19,470
and a window cannot be removed or shrunk over a booked slot.

21
00:01:19,470 --> 00:01:22,480
Those rules are covered by the automated tests,

22
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:24,980
and the booking journeys will use them.

23
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:27,910
Here is what to remember.

24
00:01:27,910 --> 00:01:32,320
Only approved providers save availability, and only their own.

25
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:37,660
Windows cannot overlap, and times are entered in Eastern Time and stored in

26
00:01:37,660 --> 00:01:38,730
universal time.

27
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:44,710
Buyers see only free slots from approved providers, and booked times are never lost.

28
00:01:44,710 --> 00:01:47,270
Next, journey four: manage vehicles.
